  body: "# Evidence for a DMG tribunal appeal\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe appeals guidance calls for relevant
    evidence available to the decision maker to be available to the tribunal and disclosed, while distinguishing
    legal advice and specific non-disclosure directions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis describes the source’s
    appeal procedure. It does not authorise publishing claimant data, legal advice or restricted papers in this
    repository. The tribunal’s directions and the specific redaction provisions qualify the general passage.\n\n\
    ## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 06286, PDF page 45](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d4adbcb60fc6ccb2a0c/dmg-vol-1-ch-6.pdf#page=45)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 6: Making appeals and staying.\n- [DMG 06288, PDF page 46](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d4adbcb60fc6ccb2a0c/dmg-vol-1-ch-6.pdf#page=46)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 6: Making appeals and staying.\n- [DMG 06296, PDF page 47](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d4adbcb60fc6ccb2a0c/dmg-vol-1-ch-6.pdf#page=47)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 6: Making appeals and staying.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source is DWP guidance,
    not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are one-based file
    positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships preserve
    extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current applicability
    remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch6` PDF SHA-256: `dcd2a7ede4499792d9bc6762c94a2d6c0ca6e811cb077abbbd4e41e4d405a4e4`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `e95434f7e856adbd1c8550b369066644a6bf6aa7567af05a1d41768d3dae0c3e`.\n\nThe publicly
    acquired chapter 6 PDF carries the printed footer “Official - DWP Use Only”. This observation is preserved alongside
    its public acquisition URL; the source owner should clarify any conflict with intended reuse. It is not evidence
    of access to unpublished material.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-first-tier-appeal
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The passage sets an evidence-disclosure context for an appeal and expressly excludes advice on
      law from evidence.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch6/0045
      quote: "06286 All evidence\n\n\n1. relevant to the appeal and\n\n\n2. available to the DM\n\n\nshould be available
        to the tribunal and disclosed to the appellant or representative 1. (see DMG Chapter\n01).\n\n\nNote: Advice
        on the law, such as guidance on an individual case, is not evidence and should not be\ndisclosed to the
        appellant, representative or tribunal. See DMG Chapter 01 for further details.\n\n\n                   \
        \                                                                               1 R(S) 1/58"
      locator: DMG 06286
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The statement-presentation guidance requires readable records and original documents where
      practicable; it is related to, but distinct from, general evidence assessment.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch6/0048
      quote: "06305 The Department should ensure that\n\n\n1. written statements are signed with an explanation
        of why they were made and signed unless the\n\nreason is self-evident1\n\n\n2. all evidence that is hard
        to read, especially records of interviews or phone calls, is typed and signed\n\n\n3. the original documents
        are available at the hearing where practicable\n\n\n4. the advice in DMG Chapter 01 about evidence given
        in confidence is followed where the evidence\nrefers to imprisonment\n\n\n5. anonymous letters are not included\n\
        \n\n6. anonymous witness statements are not routinely included. Generally a witness should not be\nanonymous
        unless there are special circumstances requiring anonymity and that would be a matter for\nthe tribunal
        chairman to decide\n\n\n7. if redacted documents are included the papers, an unredacted copy in a sealed
        envelope should be\nmade available to the chairman of the FtT.\n\n\n                                   \
        \                                                                  1 R(G) 1/63"
      locator: DMG 06305
